        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "cc90e764-9efd-359b-892c-2c500ba8b636",
                "word": "bas-bleu",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "50c58a6b-0707-319f-b93f-0c62851e2d01",
                        "entry_id": "cc90e764-9efd-359b-892c-2c500ba8b636",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif aux femmes de lettres."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0314b1c2-76f2-4029-86ca-f792efe5a848",
                                "sense_id": "50c58a6b-0707-319f-b93f-0c62851e2d01",
                                "text": "Les gens de lettres ? La plaie de la métropole. Et si l'on apprenait son passage à Londres, gare à ces dames bas-bleu, « esthétiques », artistes-amateurs, qui donnent des thés, bâclent des bouquins, et dont les filles composent des poèmes, forment un album d'autographes! « Nous n'avons rien de comparable à votre mot français raseuses ! »"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "03ae21f3-9d70-3462-9724-4346cc3351bc",
                "word": "bas-bleu",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c569be75-9b30-44bb-a106-2dc895c15cb9",
                        "entry_id": "03ae21f3-9d70-3462-9724-4346cc3351bc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bas-bleus"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "35d7c125-44c5-453d-b2fd-516851cedadb",
                        "entry_id": "03ae21f3-9d70-3462-9724-4346cc3351bc",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "bas bleu"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                        "entry_id": "03ae21f3-9d70-3462-9724-4346cc3351bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Femme à prétentions littéraires."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4fb39c17-fc88-4b3d-ad40-7829844a91e7",
                                "sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                                "text": "21 octobre 1940 – Il n’avait pas reniflé en moi le bas-bleu, la suffragette, la revendicatrice, bref la fille à fuir !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0382e7b0-3d62-4b5b-b817-103f83d2ae75",
                                "sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                                "text": "Les débutants, les bas-bleus, les actrices qui commencent et celles qui finissent leur carrière, auteurs et libraires caressent ou choyent ces plumes à tout faire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20a829fc-d762-4181-887a-c0a33fd8df5a",
                                "sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                                "text": "Si je veux observer la loi des contrastes, qui gouverne l'ordre moral et l'ordre physique, je suis obligé de ranger dans la classe des femmes dangereuses aux gens de lettres, la femme honnête, le bas-bleu et l'actrice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e70aadd-a80d-4313-871d-6c80f9e3769d",
                                "sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                                "text": "Il y aura aussi toute la jeune opposition : des journalistes, des avocats, des bas-bleus qui, de leur jarretière, étrangleraient l’empereur s’il tombait sous leurs griffes roses, et qui ont mis leur chapeau des dimanches en bataille."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "677c34e0-bc52-4344-92da-7d0efb4f0a45",
                                "sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                                "text": "En vis-à-vis du bâtiment vétuste, l’établissement des jeunes élèves-maîtresses, guindées en leur costume sévère sous le chapeau de feutre sans élégance. Le plupart portent lorgnons. Un peu bas-bleu ! pas mal pimbêches."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26642831-94d9-4690-9913-50c97e6f983d",
                                "sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                                "text": "Mais s’il aimait les femmes d’esprit, mon père n’avait aucun goût pour les bas-bleus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b42dafb-8f91-4451-b709-96bc32df8e64",
                                "sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                                "text": "Il ne s’agit ni de détourner les femmes de leur véritable vocation, qui est d’élever leurs enfants et de tenir leurs ménages, ni de les transformer en savants, en bas-bleus, en ergoteuses. » (ndlr, « bas-bleu » est expression péjorative pour désigner une femme cultivée)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0b3de99-76d1-4554-9d58-9874f090039d",
                        "source_entry_id": "03ae21f3-9d70-3462-9724-4346cc3351bc",
                        "source_sense_id": "3170c995-d195-3588-b228-689c35d819d1",
                        "source_sense_description": "Femme à prétentions littéraires",
                        "target_lang_word": "bluestocking",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bluestocking",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc65e31c-1ef7-391d-b8c5-ea63a6ee6c05",
                                        "entry_id": "5d515547-a5aa-3783-b9b2-0e0ca913d8ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A scholarly, literary, or cultured woman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "009c44b0-2378-4eb5-af46-68cc1001181f",
                                                "sense_id": "cc65e31c-1ef7-391d-b8c5-ea63a6ee6c05",
                                                "text": "Many of her ladyship’s letters were the most whimsical rhodomontades that ever blue-stocking penned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c74508d-e54a-4f75-9f64-03e9022b3417",
                                                "sense_id": "cc65e31c-1ef7-391d-b8c5-ea63a6ee6c05",
                                                "text": "But Isabel was no blue-stocking; she was full of vivacity and life, and her conversation was sprightly and agreeable, even when turning upon those serious subjects."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6706818-86f6-4951-a544-f61929a6a2d9",
                                                "sense_id": "cc65e31c-1ef7-391d-b8c5-ea63a6ee6c05",
                                                "text": "And let none cast in my teeth[…]the remark of Hippolytus in Euripides: “I detest a bluestocking. May there never be a woman in my house who knows more than is fitting for a woman to know.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35bce9aa-d617-4ba5-8209-0c4f6e5da9af",
                                                "sense_id": "cc65e31c-1ef7-391d-b8c5-ea63a6ee6c05",
                                                "text": "“Heavens!” exclaimed Nina, “the blue-stocking and the fogy!—and yours are pale blue, Eileen!—you’re about as self-conscious as Drina—slumping there with your hair tumbling à la Mérode! Oh, it’s very picturesque, of course, but a straight spine and good grooming is better.[…]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d90800e-1e72-4fd7-8ef8-35f3e626e920",
                                                "sense_id": "cc65e31c-1ef7-391d-b8c5-ea63a6ee6c05",
                                                "text": "Bragg was a Massachusetts-born bluestocking, a New Woman of the Progressive Era who changed not only the cultural face of Charleston but also the nation's approach to museum education."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e49a948-a495-4d35-95fc-61ccf79e42c5",
                                                "sense_id": "cc65e31c-1ef7-391d-b8c5-ea63a6ee6c05",
                                                "text": "The artist who created strong, passionate, brilliant heroines turns out to have disapproved of bluestockings and refused to educate his own intelligent daughters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3325f80-a52e-4d53-bccf-3393a7956486",
                                                "sense_id": "cc65e31c-1ef7-391d-b8c5-ea63a6ee6c05",
                                                "text": "But the cultural conflict between these two post-revolutionary styles — between frat guys and feminist bluestockings, Gamergaters and the diversity police, alt-right provocateurs and 'woke' dudebros, the mouthbreathers who poured hate on the all-female 'Ghostbusters' and the tastemakers who pretended it was good — is likely here to stay."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75dc31fb-90b0-3f91-a3cf-a94c17638af8",
                                        "entry_id": "5d515547-a5aa-3783-b9b2-0e0ca913d8ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of an 18th-century Blue Stockings Society."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea5b36f7-8764-3a8e-bbd2-4181e8ecf625",
                                        "entry_id": "5d515547-a5aa-3783-b9b2-0e0ca913d8ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of the English parliament of 1653, more commonly called the Barebones Parliament."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
